@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# Fixture for the literal search index under the Unicode fold
# (docs/designissues/2026-10-10-literal-index-lgi3.md). Every label below is
# matched by CONTAINS(LCASE(STR(?o)), needle) only if LCASE is the Unicode
# case mapping, and only a Unicode fold in the index lists it as a candidate.
#
#   needle      rows    reason
#   école       s1      É (U+00C9) lower-cases to é (U+00E9)
#   ecole       s7      "École Normale" lower-cases to "école normale", which
#                       does not contain "ecole"; only the ASCII label does
#   kelvin      s2      KELVIN SIGN (U+212A, written as an escape below)
#                       lower-cases to k
#   stanbul     s3      İ (U+0130) lower-cases to i + U+0307
#   οδυσσευς    s4      the final capital sigma lower-cases to ς, and the
#                       index folds both sigma forms to σ
#   straße      s5      ß is its own lower case
#   plain       s6      plain ASCII
#   unmatched   none    negative control: no label contains it
#
# The labels are in a NAMED graph, because `l4block-literal-gate` asks
# `GRAPH ?g { ?s <P> ?o FILTER(...) }` first, and a generation whose quads are
# all in the default graph answers that with no rows.
ex:g {
  ex:s1 rdfs:label "École Normale" .
  ex:s2 rdfs:label "\u212AELVIN scale" .
  ex:s3 rdfs:label "İstanbul" .
  ex:s4 rdfs:label "ΟΔΥΣΣΕΥΣ" .
  ex:s5 rdfs:label "Straße" .
  ex:s6 rdfs:label "plain label" .
  ex:s7 rdfs:label "Ecole without accent" .
}
